What was the Hardest thing to understand so far? What did you understand this week?

The hardest thing to understand so far was probably the main difference between using Euler-cromer and Verlet. 
I understand they both take really tiny time steps to see what the position of an object is doing, but it was difficult for me to understand
why use one over the other. This week, I understood that using Verlet was more useful because of its symplectic nature. Because it uses both Acceleration 
and velocity in tiny time intervals instead of just A (Euler), the small numerical errors made during the dt steps were bounded instead of accumulated.
